src/single-sided-lp/CurveConvex2Token.sol:unstakeAndExitPool|class=C22|High|On any CurveInterface.V2 vault whose Curve coin is the WETH ERC-20 (the standard crypto-v2 layout), _exitPool hardcodes use_eth=true so the pool unwraps and pushes native ETH, but the re-wrap in unstakeAndExitPool only fires when TOKEN_i == ETH_ADDRESS, so the vault treats the native ETH it received as an increase in its WETH balance — the two-sided delta tokenBalance(TOKEN_1) - before reads 0 and the redeemer is credited nothing while the ETH is stranded, and the single-sided path credits an amount of asset=WETH the vault never received and pays it out of other users' WETH until redemptions revert.|src/single-sided-lp/CurveConvex2Token.sol
